1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,460
Jira just refused to start this ticket.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,253
That's not a bug.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,094
It's a pre-flight check.

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:12,638
Every flight gets a check before it leaves the gate.

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,597
Software doesn't.

6
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,915
Written Tuesday. Shipped Thursday.

7
00:00:17,985 --> 00:00:19,935
Nobody checks what's on board.

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:23,276
Months later, a complaint lands.

9
00:00:23,346 --> 00:00:27,700
Customer ID numbers. No reason. No end date.

10
00:00:27,771 --> 00:00:29,186
And one question.

11
00:00:29,256 --> 00:00:30,532
Who approved this?

12
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,140
Regulators are already fining.

13
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:34,591
One million rand.

14
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:35,820
Half a million.

15
00:00:35,891 --> 00:00:37,701
Up to ten years in prison.

16
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:39,982
Preflight.

17
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,787
Privacy review, before you build.

18
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:47,589
Step one. The scanner.

19
00:00:47,659 --> 00:00:49,968
It reads every ticket as it's written.

20
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:51,685
Title and description.

21
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:56,682
ID numbers. Health details. Children's data.

22
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:59,275
Step two. The gate.

23
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:02,975
Personal data on board? The gate stays closed.

24
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,709
Here it is in Jira.

25
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:06,553
Drag to In Progress.

26
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:07,898
Refused.

27
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:10,034
With exactly what's missing.

28
00:01:10,104 --> 00:01:14,307
Why you need it. Your lawful basis. When it's deleted.

29
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,384
Step three. Your co-pilot.

30
00:01:17,454 --> 00:01:19,798
Ask the Preflight agent in Rovo.

31
00:01:19,869 --> 00:01:21,284
It checks the ticket.

32
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:23,481
It drafts the answer.

33
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:26,636
Then it asks before saving anything.

34
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:30,672
The draft counts only when a person clicks Use draft.

35
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:33,310
AI can help.

36
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,161
It can't approve.

37
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:40,054
Step four. The control tower.

38
00:01:40,124 --> 00:01:43,176
Approvers see every waiting ticket in one inbox.

39
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,691
Save the answers, and Approve unlocks.

40
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,512
One click.

41
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:51,805
Name, date and time, on the record.

42
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,996
Gate open. Cleared to build.

43
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,215
Now, try to sneak past.

44
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:00,619
Reword the ticket.

45
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,394
Still flagged.

46
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,711
Change an answer after sign-off.

47
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:07,833
Clearance cancelled.

48
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:10,313
It needs a new sign-off.

49
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:13,651
Step five. The landing check.

50
00:02:13,721 --> 00:02:16,007
Before Done, one more proof.

51
00:02:16,078 --> 00:02:18,771
A link to the updated privacy notice.

52
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:23,291
Every answer goes into the flight recorder.

53
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:24,670
Write-once.

54
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:26,259
So ask again.

55
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:27,856
Who approved this?

56
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,052
It's on the record.

57
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,481
The checklist is yours.

58
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:36,182
Start with POPIA or GDPR.

59
00:02:36,252 --> 00:02:39,572
Or let Rovo draft rules from your own policy.

60
00:02:39,642 --> 00:02:42,834
Nothing is enforced until an approver switches it on.

61
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:44,912
Preflight.

62
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,717
Privacy review, before you build.
